new file mode 100644
index 000000000..310bb3da8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/en/dev/language/tile-compact-compare.md
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Paired compare compaction (local A3 prototype)
+
+`pl.tile.compact_compare(src, threshold, scratch, offset, cmp_mode="ge",
+out_cols=capacity)` returns three SSA values: packed FP32 values, INT32 column
+indices, and exact per-row INT32 counts. It is a Tile-level operation inside an
+InCore function; a Tensor-level convenience API is not provided.
+
+Selection is stable and moves FP32 bit representations without conversion.
+Indices use `offset + source_column` in INT32 arithmetic; offset is a device
+Scalar and must not overflow INT32 when combined with the source column.
+Predicates `eq`, `gt` and `ge` are supported by this prototype.
+
+Source physical columns must be divisible by 64. Output capacity is divisible by
+8 and no larger than source columns. Source valid rows and columns can vary at
+runtime. Each output row defines only `min(count, capacity)` prefix entries;
+tails are undefined. Count is never truncated, and overflow does not write
+beyond the output allocation. Count storage has shape
+`[1, align_up(source_rows, 8)]`, with logical valid shape `[1, source_rows]`.
+
+Scratch is a UINT8 Tile requiring
+`4*C + max(1024, align_up(C,256)/8 + 4*C)` bytes for physical source width `C`.
+It is explicitly marked as a workspace and cannot be used as a hidden output.
+The three results use the existing multi-output allocation and tuple projection
+infrastructure. Generic `create_op_call` bindings need no new nanobind entry.
+
+PTO codegen emits `pto.tcompact.compare`, so the matching local PTOAS extension
+is required. The extension provides a Vector implementation, Scalar count
+effects, capacity checks and synchronization modeling. This documentation does
+not imply upstream availability, A5 support or measured performance benefit.
